# Screenshot smoke (mandatory before "ready")

## Rule

**Never tell Steve the game or study server is ready** until Playwright screenshot smoke passes and you **paste screenshot paths** (or images) in chat.

Applies to **`npm run dev`** and **`npm run dev:study`** — study mode only disables HMR; it does **not** skip screenshot smoke.

```powershell
Set-Location C:\Users\steve\MeWorld\game
npm run dev          # or: npm run dev:study
# servers already up:
npm run smoke:differential-session
npm run smoke:play-case
```

To skip browser smoke only when debugging: `SKIP_PLAY_SMOKE=1` or `--skip-play-smoke` on `start-dev.mjs` — **not** the default for study.

## What must pass

| Script | Screenshots | Catches |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `smoke-differential-session.mjs` | `docs/smoke-screenshots/<date>/01-welcome.png` … `06-floating-chat-open.png` | White blank differential |
| `smoke-play-case-session.mjs` | `docs/smoke-screenshots/<date>/play-case/*.png` | Black/white welcome, briefing, play, **Continue**, **The Whys**, **`?case=U01`** |

Play-case flow includes:

1. Welcome + blank-screen guards (`smoke-screen-utils.mjs`)
2. Continue panel (uber case in seeded history)
3. The Whys panel
4. Play → briefing → play scene
5. Uber **U01** deep-link (missing import / null vitals regressions)
6. **Settings toggles** — Timed ON/OFF and Simulate deterioration ON/OFF (`settings-popover-btn--on`, `aria-pressed`)

## Button & toggle smoke (mandatory)

During play-case smoke, **click every toggle both ways** before calling dev ready:

| Control | Verify |
|---------|--------|
| Timed / Untimed | `aria-pressed` + `settings-popover-btn--on` when ON |
| Simulate deterioration | Same — label flips `Deterioration: ON` |
| Any new toolbar button | Click ON and OFF (or open/close) — screenshot both states |

If a button has no visible pressed/disabled state when clicked, **fix the UI** before shipping — do not skip because smoke “passed” visually.

**Chat thread persistence** is covered separately (Pass D in `docs/smoke-play-pass-checklist.md`) — no extra smoke unless chat storage changes.

## Study snapshot

`START-MEWORLD-STUDY.bat` runs **frozen** `MeWorld-study`. After fixes on main:

```powershell
cd C:\Users\steve\MeWorld
powershell -File scripts\create-study-snapshot.ps1
```

Black screen on study = stale snapshot or skipped smoke. Refresh snapshot; do not patch only `MeWorld-study`.

## Common failures

| Symptom | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Black screen | `node scripts/audit-game-case-load.mjs` · uber vitals in `caseNarrative.js` · missing `gameData.js` imports |
| White screen | `npm run smoke:pre-serve` (vite build) |
| `enrichUberGameCase is not defined` | Import from `uberCases.js` in `gameData.js` |
| **`smoke:play-case` times out on `.game-scene`** | **NOT flaky.** Two distinct causes, both fixed — diagnose before re-labeling: (1) portrait **auto-regeneration (~90s)** on load — regen is now **manual-only**, load serves cache (incl. banned via `allowBanned`); verify `POST /api/regenerate-patient-from-case` `refresh:false` → `cached:true` <1s. (2) **Play.jsx render crash → blank scene** (e.g. temporal-dead-zone: a `useMemo`/`useEffect` referencing a `useState` declared further down, like `orderTimelineEvents`). Open the play scene in the browser and read `window` errors — a `ReferenceError: Cannot access 'X' before initialization` = move the hook **below** the state declaration. Do **not** re-label as "known flaky scene-selector." |
| `smoke:play-case` times out clicking **settings / Timed / Deterioration** toggle (`.toolbar-settings-popover` click "intercepted" by `.case-treatment-stacks`) | The settings popover lives in the order-timeline foot inside `.game-scene-capture` (`z-index:1`), which traps its stacking **below** the floating sidebar (`z-index:30`). Popover is **portaled to `<body>`** (`PlaySceneToolbar.jsx` → `.toolbar-settings-portal`, z 4000) so it renders above the sidebar; outside-click handler in `Play.jsx` ignores clicks inside `.toolbar-settings-popover`. The order-timeline **foot stays visible when the list is collapsed** (`PatientOrderTimeline.jsx`) so the toolbar is always reachable. Don't re-nest the popover or re-gate the foot on `!collapsed`. |
| `smoke:play-case` fails **"no page errors"** with `401` on `/api/detect-zones` | Vision zone-detection is optional. When `OPENAI_API_KEY` is missing/expired the endpoint now **degrades to HTTP 200 + `{zones:null, skipped:true}`** instead of forwarding OpenAI's 401 to the browser console. If you see 401 again, the graceful-skip in `server/index.js` `POST /api/detect-zones` was reverted. Restart the API after editing — it does **not** hot-reload. |
| Study still broken after main fix | Re-run `create-study-snapshot.ps1` |

Pair with: `meworld-game-data-imports.mdc` · `play-case-chat.mdc`
